N smileplot.pkg
D  9 Jun 2026
U 9
d 'SMILEPLOT': module to create plots for use with multiple significance tests
d 
d  This package contains the programs multproc, smileplot and
d smileplot7.     multproc inputs a data set with 1 observation
d for each of a set of multiple       significance tests and data
d on the P-values, and carries out a multiple test  procedure
d chosen by the user to define a corrected overall critical P-value
d for accepting or rejecting the null hypotheses tested.
d These procedures  may be one-step, step-up or step-down, and
d may control the familywise error  rate (eg the Bonferroni,
d Sidak, Holm, Holland-Copenhaver, Hochberg and Rom
d procedures) or the false discovery rate (eg the Simes,
d Benjamini-Liu,       Benjamini-Yekutieli and
d Benjamini-Krieger-Yekutieli procedures). smileplot,     and its
d Stata 7 version smileplot7, work by calling multproc and then
d   creating a smile plot, with data points corresponding to
d multiple estimated    parameters, the P-values (on a reverse
d log scale) on the Y-axis, and the   corresponding parameter
d estimates (or another variable) on the X-axis. There      are
d Y-axis reference lines at the uncorrected and corrected overall
d critical  P-values. The reference line at the corrected
d critical P-value, known as the       parapet line, is interpreted
d informally as a boundary between data mining and  data
d dredging. multproc, smileplot and smileplot7 are used on data
d sets with   one observation per estimated parameter and data
d on estimates and their       P-values, which may be created using
d parmby, parmest, statsby or postfile.
d 
d KW: plot
d KW: multiple analyses
d KW: multiple significance tests
d 
d Requires: Stata version 10.0
d 
d Distribution-Date: 20121011
d 
d Author: Roger Newson, National Heart and Lung Institute, Imperial College London
d Support: email r.newson@@imperial.ac.uk
d 
f s\smileplot.ado
f s\smileplot.sthlp
f s\smileplot7.ado
f s\smileplot7.sthlp
f m\multproc.ado
f m\multproc.sthlp
e
